{"name":"Sassy","hex":"#c18862","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sassy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A diminutive of the female given name Saskia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sassy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sassy (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sassy is an album by the American jazz vocalist Sarah Vaughan with Hal Mooney and his orchestra, recorded in 1956 and released on the EmArcy label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Sassy_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sassy_(album)"},{"title":"Pretty on the Inside","blocks":[{"text":"Pretty on the Inside is the debut studio album by American alternative rock band Hole, released on September 17, 1991, in the United States on Caroline Records. Produced by Sonic Youth's Kim Gordon, and Gumball frontman Don Fleming, the album was Hole's first major label release after the band's formation in 1989 by vocalist, songwriter, and guitarist Courtney Love and lead guitarist Eric Erlandson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Hole_-_Pretty_on_the_Inside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretty_on_the_Inside"},{"title":"Sassy (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Sassy magazine was a general interest teen magazine aimed at young women. Now defunct, it covered a wide variety of topics, and was intended as a feminist counterpoint to Seventeen and YM magazines. Sassy existed between 1988 and 1996."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f4/SassymagCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sassy_(magazine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/POTI_Interior.png/330px-POTI_Interior.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai